        },
        {
          "type": "real",
          "name": "melee death acceleration#acceleration applied to a biped when killed by a melee.  0 defaults to 1.6"
        },
        {
          "type": "real",
          "name": "uber melee death acceleration#acceleration applied to a biped when killed by an uber melee.  0 defaults to 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "custom",
          "name": "clang",
          "group_tag": "fgrb"
        },
        {
          "type": "explanation",
          "name": "clang",
          "definition": "This occurs when one person does melee damage to another unit performing a melee that could hit the other unit\nand either unit has no vitality remaining\n\ncase both units have no vitality remaining:\nif the abolute value of the difference between the units vitality is less than \"simultaneous death vitality threshold\", then both will die\notherwise whoever has more health will be saved (brought down to near 0 vitality) and the other will get killed\n\ncase only 1 unit has no vitality remaining:\nthe unit with no vitality is killed, and the other unit's vitality isn't modified from the clang"
        },
        {
          "type": "explanation",
          "name": "Network sensitive fields",
          "definition": "WARNING these affects how melees over network.\nDon't modify without consulting weapon or network engineer.\nThese are hidden by default and must be modified in expert mode."
        },
        {
          "type": "real",
          "name": "clang simultaneous death vitality threshold!#Defaults to 0.59.  Halo 3 had a value of 0.59 (the average of damage caused by 4 BR and 4 AR bullets worth of damage which is roughly 26.5 damage out of a body health of 45).  Reach had 1.1 so they both would die if both had no shields since there was no bleed through."
        },
        {
          "type": "custom",
          "name": null,
          "group_tag": "fgre"
        },
        {
          "type": "real",
          "name": "input hold time#length of time that separates early release melee actions, e.g. melee vs ground pound when in the air (defaults to 0.25)"
        },
